## 4. Profiles: other companies and alternatives

### Posh: strongest product threat
- **What it is:** an algorithm-driven event feed ("TikTok for events") personalized by past attendance and contacts. It has nearly 6M users and ~50K organizers, has processed $300M+ in ticket sales, keeps 10% of ticket sales, made $10M in revenue in 2024 and has raised $40M [[1]](#sources).
- **Implication:** a personalized feed alone won't set us apart. Crew Blend and Demand Signals have to.

### Spotify: threat to our positioning
- **What it is:** a weekly **Concerts Near You** playlist based on your listening, launched March 2025 [[2]](#sources), and a daily **Live Events feed** with 20K+ venues you can follow, launched October 2025 [[3]](#sources).
- **Implication:** "Spotify for local events" invites a direct comparison with Spotify's own feature. Position ourselves on non-music scenes and groups.

### Bandsintown
- **What it is:** concert alerts and artist tracking for 100M+ fans, 700K artists and 45K venues [[13]](#sources). Fans can **request** that artists play their city [[4]](#sources).
- **Implication:** a partial precedent for Demand Signals. Ours covers any event format, not just artists, and shows hosts the size and location of the matched audience.

### Resident Advisor and EDMtrain
- **What they are:** deep electronic-music discovery in Toronto. RA lists 266+ upcoming Toronto events with "For you" and "RA Picks" sections [[11]](#sources). EDMtrain offers artist tracking, genre filters and Spotify/Apple Music integration [[12]](#sources).
- **Implication:** strong within one scene, but they're the "too niche" problem.

### Showpass and blogTO
- **What they are:** Showpass is Canadian ticketing with Toronto discovery pages such as "Popular in Toronto" and "This weekend" [[10]](#sources). blogTO runs free, community-submitted event listings [[19]](#sources).
- **Implication:** potential **supply partners** for event data rather than head-on rivals.

### Partiful
- **What it is:** a party invitation app popular with people under 30, used in 100+ countries. It raised a $20M Series A and has **no revenue model** [[14]](#sources).
- **Borrow:** invites that work without an app download; group polls.

### Timeleft
- **What it is:** paid dinners with strangers, now also bars and running groups. It has 150K diners a month in 200+ cities and €18M ARR [[15]](#sources).
- **Implication:** a model for a paid **"Crew Night"** for solo attendees like Jordan.

### Meetup
- **What it is:** interest-based groups with 60M+ registered members, acquired by Bending Spoons in 2024 [[16]](#sources).
- **Implication:** covers community groups (a host type for us) but not personal taste.

### Radiate
- **What it is:** a community app for festival and electronic music fans, with event group chats and a "Hey" feature for connecting with other attendees [[17]](#sources).
- **Borrow:** "who's going" and event chats for our Event day hub.

### Instagram, TikTok, group chats and Google
- **What they are:** the default way many people find events today. A 2026 study of Gen Z festival-goers found **content from other attendees influences decisions more than influencers**, and socializing with friends was a top reason to go [[18]](#sources).
- **Implication:** our real competition is habit. Make Crew Blend plans easy to share back into group chats and Instagram.

